---


AxiorHub Pilot reads the firm’s mailbox and case files, understands what is coming in, and **prepares the work**:
reply drafts, draft legal documents, exhibit lists, deadlines, and tasks. It never sends anything, signs anything, or
files anything. Every deliverable is a draft or a project that the attorney reviews, corrects, and approves.

This software was created for french solo attorneys or small firms by Timo RAINIO.

| | |
|---|---|
| **Who it is for** | Solo attorneys or small firms, together with their associates and assistants. |
| **Where** | On the firm’s own server (a VPS is sufficient): the mailbox and Nextcloud remain yours. |
| **Which AI** | Local (Ollama), external (Anthropic, OpenAI, Mistral…) **pseudonymized**, or both. |
| **What it never does** | Send an email, sign, file, unilaterally set a procedural date, or invent a source. |

## What the agent does

### The control station

The “Today” screen brings together everything that requires the attorney’s attention:

- an **input area**: “Prepare the reply to opposing counsel about the procedural timetable in the LEROY case.”
  The agent infers the relevant case file, which you can correct. You can attach a document or dictate (microphone);
- **To review**: ready-to-open email drafts and document projects, one click away;
- **What the agent is doing**: work in progress, completed, or blocked, with the name of the document or request being handled;
- **My day**: today’s hearings and appointments, Nextcloud tasks (both the agent’s and yours), and the Deck board;
- **Routines**: morning briefing, morning email triage, weekly review;
- **Firm style**: proposed writing habits, for approval.

A banner at the bottom of the page shows the agent’s activity in real time. A dark mode is available.

### Review and approve in one click

<p align="center"><img src="docs/captures/02-relecture-projet.png" alt="Review panel for a draft pleading" width="900"></p>

Each project opens in a panel: full text, cited sources, and “TO BE COMPLETED” items. You can:
- **approve** the project;
- **dismiss** it;
- **open it in the editor** (Word online via OnlyOffice) or in Nextcloud;
- request a **new version** with a single sentence (“firmer tone”, “add the hearing date”).

The agent learns from these decisions.

### Know exactly what the agent is doing

<p align="center"><img src="docs/captures/03-detail-travail.png" alt="Details of an agent task" width="900"></p>

Each task opens with its details:
- the case file;
- the document analyzed, the requested document, or the relevant email;
- the steps completed and the result;
- links to open the generated file;
- a “Retry” button if the task is blocked.

The “Why is nothing being produced?” screen explains any failure: services, work queue, errors and their causes,
connections, and automated checks.

### Emails

- **Triage** of incoming messages: client email, opposing counsel, court, RPVA notification, advertising,
  mailing list, automated message.
- **Assignment to the correct case file** based on correspondents, references, and history; when in doubt, a
  proposal is made, and a confirmed association is then used for subsequent messages.
- **Reply drafts** placed in the Drafts folder of your mailbox (IMAP), within the original thread,
  with your signature. Nothing is sent.
- **“Emails to review” workspace**:
  - edit the text, recipient, and subject;
  - dictate corrections by voice;
  - request a rewrite (“shorter”, “more courteous”, “add a reminder of the date”);
  - check legal citations;
  - save a rule: “always do it this way”.
- **Mailbox** (“Inbox” tab under “Emails”): mailbox folders (inbox, sent, drafts, trash, subfolders), side-by-side
  list and reading view, readable attachments; “Ask the agent for a reply” for a selected email, with an existing case
  file, without a case file, or by creating a new one, together with an instruction and the text of the attachments.
  Prepared replies can be edited, deleted, or regenerated with an instruction.
- **Email functions**: reply, reply all, forward, new message (To, Cc, Bcc, formatted text, attachments), archive,
  move, mark as spam, delete (trash), read / unread, follow.
- **Sending** is disabled by default. If enabled, it requires a confirmation summarizing the recipients, subject, and
  attachments.
- **Why no draft?** Every unprocessed email states the reason (firm message, mailing list, uncertain case file,
  attorney decision required…) and the action needed to fix it.

### Documents and draft legal documents

- **Natural-language request**: pleadings, summons, application, letter, formal notice, memorandum, legal opinion,
  contract. The draft is prepared from the case file (exhibits, facts, chronology) and the **firm’s templates**.
- **Automatic filing** in the case-file folder structure (PROCEDURE, CORRESPONDENCE, PROJECTS, DELIVERABLES).
- **New versions** on instruction, without overwriting the original, including for a document you wrote yourself.
- **Online editing** of the Word document in the browser (OnlyOffice), with no download required.

### Exhibits and exhibit lists

- Reads the case-file PDFs and proposes an **order**, **captions**, and **dates**.
- **Numbering** and a “Exhibit No. X” **stamp** on the pages, plus a Word and PDF **exhibit list** based on your template.
- A **single PDF** with one bookmark per exhibit.
- **Renumbered cross-references** in the pleadings, with tracked changes.
- **Splitting for e-Barreau filing** according to the maximum upload size.
- Everything is done locally, without AI, and only after your confirmation code. Original files are never modified.

### Deadlines, calendar and tasks

- **Procedural notices** (adjournment, summons, timetable): dates are extracted and checked against the text,
  added to the Nextcloud calendar, and an information email is prepared.
- **Procedural deadlines**: the triggering event (service, notification, notice of appeal…) is identified in the
  document. The time limit is calculated using deterministic rules, never by AI. Each date is proposed “to be
  confirmed” together with its calculation, then reminders are issued in cascade.
- **Limitation periods and time bars**: versioned rules with their statutory provisions and a detailed step-by-step calculation.
- **Add an event** from “Calendar and tasks”, to one or more configured calendars (Nextcloud, CalDAV, Google Calendar),
  with review of each entry.
- **Tasks**: a simple list grouped by due date (overdue, today, this week, later, no due date),
  with filters by period and case file, and the ability to add a task right there.
- **Nextcloud calendar and tasks** (CalDAV) and **Deck**: a work plan by case file, agent tasks and
  personal tasks, and cards that track the progress of each deliverable.

### Case files

- **Case-file page**: one clear page. The working summary prepared by the agent provides the overview, a written recap
  of the facts, the parties to the dispute (capacity, counsel, firm client), the proceedings, and a chronology of the
  key events, each item linked to its exhibits; the attorney can correct it directly. Alongside: work with the agent
  within the case file (letter, memorandum, pleadings, question), parties, proceedings, and recent emails.
- **Per-case agent control**: “Pause the AI” (no further automatic work), permanent instructions followed by the agent,
  and automatic retries suspended after three consecutive failures.
- **Unified chronology** (emails, exhibits, filings, hearings).
- **Case facts** extracted from the exhibits (case number, amounts, dates, parties), each with its source, for validation.
- **Search** across the entire firm (emails, documents, case files).
- **Meeting preparation**: a sourced briefing before the meeting and a draft minutes document afterwards.

### Practice management

- **Time and fees**: time entries proposed from actual activity, counted only once approved;
  budgets and alerts.
- **Conflicts of interest**: searches for parties across existing case files, with a sourced report; no work is produced
  for a new matter until the attorney has decided.
- **Traceable legal research**: a decision is cited only after verification against the official source.
- **Hearing preparation** and analysis of opposing submissions (supervised drafts).

### Firm style

The agent reads your final documents (procedural documents, correspondence, drafts) and your sent emails, then proposes
your habits: opening and closing formulas, the usual structure of pleadings, and recurring phrases. Once approved,
they are applied to drafts and documents. No sentence containing a name, number, or address is retained.

### External AI, but pseudonymized

<p align="center"><img src="docs/captures/04-pseudonymisation.png" alt="Preview of pseudonymization before sending to an external AI" width="900"></p>

Before anything is sent to a non-local AI, names, companies, addresses, phone numbers, email addresses, IBANs, and
other numbers are replaced with placeholders (`[PERSON_1]`, `[COMPANY_1]`…). The mapping table remains on the server,
and the response is restored locally. The **preview** shows exactly what would be sent. Three modes are available:
- **everything local**;
- **hybrid**: triage and reading locally, drafting via the API;
- **everything via the API**, for a VPS without a graphics card.

**External fallback** (optional): if the local model takes more than 3 minutes on a drafting task or one of your requests, or if the request has
waited in the queue too long, it is assigned to the first available provider (Mistral, then Claude, ChatGPT, OpenRouter), always
pseudonymized. Email triage and checks remain local.

